{
 "version": 1,
 "name": "bridge",
 "archetype": "infrastructure.bridge",
 "description": "A girder road bridge: a concrete deck slab on precast I-girders with an asphalt carriageway (centre and edge lines), a raised footway and an edge beam with a steel railing on each side, a row of piers under it (rounded columns on a pile cap with a hammerhead crosshead and bearings under every girder, and a diaphragm between the girders) and a stone-faced abutment with a backwall at each end. The deck is the walking and driving surface and the piers stand on the ground.",
